In the interference pattern formed by a diffraction grating, the fringe separation increases when:
(i)	the grating spacing decreases (i.e. more lines per unit length);
(ii)	the wavelength of light increases (i.e. frequency decreases);
(iii)	the distance between the grating and the screen increases.
∴ (1) and (3) are correct. (2) is incorrect.
